A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Wedding Banquet, the Lowest Seat and Banquet Invitation, the Rich Fool, and the Tower and the Warring King are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. This parable makes no use of their meanings, and they make none of this one.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus answers a guest’s remark about eating bread in the kingdom of God with a story of a great supper. The servant says, “Come; for all things are now ready,” the bidden give excuses, and the master of the house, angry, sends for others and then for more, that his house may be filled. Jesus gives no explanation and names none of the parts; the closing statement says that none of those men which were bidden shall taste of the supper.'))
